:: Day Report [interaction] {"position":"575,2500","size":"100,100"}
/* Her end-of-day report: the "How was your day?" card of the NPC Interaction screen (id dayReport, Define Interactions).
   How it works is in "End-of-day report" in Define NPCs. She sums up today's log, one line per entry, in her own words,
   and I can pick any entry that has a passage to hear it in full: its POV passage plays, and <<EndPov>> brings me back
   here ($povReturn). The first visit of the day gives the Relation and the summary (_npc.reportDay); coming back from a
   POV passage only shows the list again. */
<<silent>>
<<set _npc to ($interactionCharacter == "mom" ? $mom : $sister)>>
<<set _drEntries to setup.dayReportEntries(_npc)>>
<<set _drFirst to (_npc.reportDay !== $date.dayCount)>>
<<run State.variables[_npc.sysName].reportDay = State.variables.date.dayCount>>
<<set _drOpen to _drEntries.filter((r) => r.passage && !r.heard)>>
<<set _drStat to (_npc.sysName == "mom" ? "MomRelation" : "SisterRelation")>>
<</silent>>
<<if _drFirst>>
	<<if _npc.sysName == "mom">>
		<<if random(0, 1) == 0>>
		When I ask about her day, $mom.callName looks up as if I've handed her something. She smooths her skirt over her knees and starts at the beginning, the way she used to tell $dad.callName about hers over dinner, back when he still asked.
		<<else>>
		I ask how her day was, and she actually stops what she's doing to think about it. She has been waiting for somebody to ask since lunch, and now that I have, she wants to get it right.
		<</if>>
	<<else>>
		<<if random(0, 1) == 0>>
		I ask how her day was, and $sister.callName lights up like I've opened a tab she has kept open all afternoon. She pulls her feet up, gets comfortable and holds up one finger. She has a list.
		<<else>>
		She's been waiting for this. I can tell, because she starts talking before I've finished the question, stops, clears her throat with a lot of ceremony and starts over, properly this time.
		<</if>>
	<</if>>

	<<set _msgs to _drEntries.map((r) => ({ who: _npc, text: r.line }))>>
	<<Chat _msgs>>

	<<UpdateStat "+" _drStat 1>>
<<else>>
	<<if _drOpen.length > 0>>
		<<= _npc.callName>> is still there, waiting to see if I want to hear more.
	<<else>>
		That's everything, as far as <<= _npc.callName>> is concerned. She looks pleased with herself for remembering all of it.
	<</if>>
<</if>>

<<if _drOpen.length > 0>>
<div class="dr-list">
	<<for _dr range _drOpen>>
		<<capture _dr>>
		<div class="navigation-link"><<link _dr.ask>>
			<<set State.variables[_npc.sysName].dayLog[_dr.index].heard to true>>
			<<set $povReturn to "Day Report">>
			<<goto _dr.passage>>
		<</link>></div>
		<</capture>>
	<</for>>
</div>
<</if>>

<div class="navigation-link"><<link "That's enough for today" "NPC Interaction">><</link>></div>
